{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00687",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.2,
      "end_seconds": 15.34,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I got this letter about my eyes, the screening, the photos, and I've brought it but I can't find my glasses, so I can't read it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.66,
      "end_seconds": 29.63,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "No problem, I've got the result on screen. The screening shows early changes at the back of your eyes from the diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.49,
      "end_seconds": 37.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Oh no. Does that mean I'm going blind? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.16,
      "end_seconds": 50.89,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "No, not at all. It's the earliest stage, called background retinopathy. Tiny changes in the small blood vessels, and your vision isn't affected yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.68,
      "end_seconds": 57.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Right. Well, I do get blurry some days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.27,
      "end_seconds": 61.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Tell me about the blurriness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.04,
      "end_seconds": 74.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.24,
      "text": "Mostly the afternoon, when I've been at the computer. Things go fuzzy for a bit, then clear up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.91,
      "end_seconds": 80.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Any floaters, or flashing lights?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.95,
      "end_seconds": 89.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "No flashing. A few floaters, I think, but they've been there for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.4,
      "end_seconds": 98.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "Any pain in your eyes, or loss of part of your vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.62,
      "end_seconds": 104.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "No, no pain. No loss, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.03,
      "end_seconds": 111.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Now the diabetes treatment. What are you taking for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.97,
      "end_seconds": 129.02,
      "duration_seconds": 15.05,
      "text": "Metformin. 1000 mg, twice a day, I think. I'm honestly not sure of the dose, my wife organises it. And if I'm honest, I miss the evening one a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.41,
      "end_seconds": 140.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "So the plan is twice a day, 1000 mg as you recall it, but some evenings it's missed. That's honest, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.59,
      "end_seconds": 148.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "I don't want to get a row. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.78,
      "end_seconds": 162.88,
      "duration_seconds": 11.1,
      "text": "No row. It's the control that matters, so we'll try to make it easier. Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.64,
      "end_seconds": 179.22,
      "duration_seconds": 14.58,
      "text": "Sulfa drugs, but only as a child. I came out in a rash, and I've never had one since. They told my mum to keep me away from them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.06,
      "end_seconds": 186.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "Thank you. Let me check your pulse and pressure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.25,
      "end_seconds": 190.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Please, go on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.38,
      "end_seconds": 207.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Pulse 78, blood pressure 136 over 84."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.23,
      "end_seconds": 210.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Good? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.92,
      "end_seconds": 220.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Good enough. For the eyes, the best treatment is good control of your sugar and blood pressure. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.13,
      "end_seconds": 226.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "I'll try, I promise. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.8,
      "end_seconds": 240.69,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an HbA1c blood test, to see how your sugar has averaged over the last three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.56,
      "end_seconds": 246.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Right. And what about my eyes? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.91,
      "end_seconds": 256.04,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "You'll be invited for screening again in twelve months, and we'll catch any change early. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.85,
      "end_seconds": 262.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Twelve months. Good, that's not too soon. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.96,
      "end_seconds": 275.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "And for the evening metformin, try taking it with your evening meal, rather than later, or set a phone alarm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.98,
      "end_seconds": 283.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "I can set an alarm. My wife will love that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.81,
      "end_seconds": 295.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Make sure you get your eyes checked at the optician too, and find those glasses. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.24,
      "end_seconds": 301.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "They're probably in the fridge. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.38,
      "end_seconds": 307.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "It's happened before. Mind how you go. ~"
    }
  ]
}
